>DDSCAT allocating     3.81 MB for SCRRS2; total=    70.19 MB                 
>TARGET: Sphere, 179944 dipoles, 1.000 1.000 1.000=x,y,z lattice spacing   
           179944 = NAT0 = number of dipoles in target
>TARGET  NCOMP_NEED=   1 compositions in target                               
>DDSCAT returned from TARGET:                                                 
>DDSCAT : dimensions of physical target                                       
>DDSCAT    -35    34 = min, max values of JX                                  
>DDSCAT    -35    34 = min, max values of JY                                  
>DDSCAT    -35    34 = min, max values of JZ                                  
>DDSCAT X0(1-3) = location/d of lattice site (0,0,0)                          
>DDSCAT    0.50000   0.50000   0.50000 = X0(1-3)                              
>DDSCAT XCM(1-3) = location/d of centroid                                     
>DDSCAT    0.00000   0.00000   0.00000 = XCM(1-3)                             
>DDSCAT  --- physical extent of target volume (occupied sites) ---            
>DDSCAT    -35.00000    35.00000 = min, max values of x/d                     
>DDSCAT    -35.00000    35.00000 = min, max values of y/d                     
>DDSCAT    -35.00000    35.00000 = min, max values of z/d                     
>EXTEND target extent in x,y,z directions =   70,   70,   70 (in Target Frame)
